From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Scroll and tap the way iOS 6 delivers touches

Scrollable overflow areas and frames are scrolled by touch through the system's
UIWebOverflowScrollView. Touch-derived pointer events are dispatched for media
control taps, and the mouse events derived from touches are tagged as synthetic
taps so they do not double the pointer stream. The port's event and layout
adaptations are carried, inspector-only layout work is skipped, and the layout
log is restored.
